      "math_academy_id": "q-6510",
      "knowledge_point_id": "e49e2595-62a1-595a-8df9-99541bccbdf5",
      "knowledge_point": "Calculating Permutations",
      "problem": "How many permutations are there for the letters in the word \"MATH\"?",
      "worked_solution": "In the word \"MATH\" there are a total of $4$ letters with no repeating letters, so there are $4!$ ways of arranging them:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4! & =4\\times 3\\times 2\\times 1 \\\\  & =24.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, there are $24$ possible arrangements of the letters of the word \"MATH\".",
